drm/kconfig: give the apercel helper tristates a prompt

DRM_EXEC, DRM_GEM_SHMEM_HELPER and DRM_SCHED are prompt-less (hidden)
tristates in this tree, so a user value for them is discarded by
olddefconfig and the gpu-sched/drm-exec/drm-shmem-helper modules can
never be built -- yet the apercel out-of-tree GPU driver imports their
symbols. Add a prompt (and default m) to each so they become ordinary
settable tristates.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/Kconfig
@@ -212,7 +212,8 @@
           If in doubt, say "N".
 
 config DRM_EXEC
-	tristate
+	tristate "DRM execution context helper (module, for apercel)"
+	default m
 	depends on DRM
 	help
 	  Execution context for command submissions
@@ -244,7 +245,8 @@
 	  Choose this if you need the GEM DMA helper functions
 
 config DRM_GEM_SHMEM_HELPER
-	tristate
+	tristate "DRM GEM shmem helper (module, for apercel)"
+	default m
 	depends on DRM && MMU
 	help
 	  Choose this if you need the GEM shmem helper functions
@@ -254,7 +256,8 @@
 	depends on DRM
 
 config DRM_SCHED
-	tristate
+	tristate "DRM GPU scheduler (module, for apercel)"
+	default m
 	depends on DRM
 
 source "drivers/gpu/drm/i2c/Kconfig"
